{
  "Rooms, people and any other kind of resource: they colour the appointments, split the columns into groups (nested, or under each date), say when each one works and when nothing may be put in.": "",
  "Resources": "",
  "`resources` lists the kinds. An appointment holds an item's value in the kind's `field`; with `allowMultiple`, a list (one meeting, two people). The kind marked `useColorAsDefault` colours the appointments (else the first kind whose item has a colour); an appointment's own `color` wins. The tooltip names its items, and the form has a picker for each kind.": "",
  "`groups` splits the columns: each item of the first kind, then each of the next under it (`parentExpr` keeps a person under their own room). The day, week, work week and month views show a head per level. `groupByDate` turns it round: each day, with the groups under it. A drag (or Alt + Shift + arrows) to another group changes the resource: in a list, only the group's own value changes.": "",
  "A head of your own": "",
  "`resourceHeaderTemplate` draws a group's head: any MotifJS component, made for each head with the item, its name, colour, level and (by date) the date.": "",
  "Availability": "",
  "An item's own work hours and days (`workStartHour`, `workEndHour`, `workDays`) shade its columns. `blockedTimes` blocks a time, once or by a rule, for every resource or the ones named. `allowOffHours: false` keeps what the user moves or saves inside the work hours, `allowOverlap: false` keeps it off another appointment of its group; a function there decides it all. A box being moved shows where it may not go, and the form says why it cannot save.": "",
  "A kind's `items` may be a data source: it is loaded once and followed (a filter, an added room). Appointments from a data source group the same way; with `remoteFiltering`, grouped by a field of one value, the source is asked for the resources shown too (`rangeFilter` with `resources`).": "",
  "Moves it to the group before or after; Enter saves, Escape takes it back. Mirrored right to left.": "",
  "Over every column: the days of each group (by date, the groups of each day).": "",
  "A cell reads its group before its time (\"Atlas, Ana Silva, Monday 26 October, 09:00\") and a blocked time after it (\"not available: Lunch\").": "",
  "The heads of the groups are drawn only (`aria-hidden`): every cell names its group.": "",
  "Moving by the keys says where it would go, its group, and whether it is free there.": "",
  "Units: a group’s head at each level, and its item’s colour before the name.": "",
  "Unit: the line between groups (by date, between days), down the heads and the cells.": "",
  "A cell in a blocked time, and a layer over it (a hatch).": "",
  "Unit: the mark on a box where it may not go (with the `appointment` unit’s `invalid` state).": "",
  "Units: an item’s colour in the form’s pickers and the tooltip; the tooltip’s lines of resources.": "",
  "`data-level`, `data-edge`; cells `data-edge`, `data-blocked`.": "",
  "The kinds of resources the appointments use. Each colours them, may group the columns and gets a picker in the form.": "",
  "The resource fields the columns are grouped by, outer first (`['roomId', 'ownerIds']`). A view’s own `groups` wins; `[]` there for none.": "",
  "The groups stand under each date, not the dates under each group. A view’s own wins.": "",
  "Draws a group’s head in place of its name.": "",
  "Times nothing may be put in: `{ start, end, text?, allDay?, recurrenceRule?, resources? }`. Shaded on the days shown; with `resources`, only for those.": "",
  "Whether what the user moves, resizes or saves may overlap another appointment of its group (any one, without groups). A function decides the whole check: `true` when the time is free.": "",
  "Whether the user may put an appointment outside the work hours (of its resources, else the scheduler’s).": "",
  "On a focused appointment, grouped: moves it to the group before or after.": "",
  "SchedulerResource": "",
  "The appointment field that holds the item’s value (`roomId`), or a list of them (`ownerIds`).": "",
  "the field": "",
  "The form’s label; how the cells and the tooltip name the kind.": "",
  "The items, in memory or from a data source (loaded once, then followed). Your data may be plain or reactive; the component reads it as it is. After changing it in place, call `refreshResources()` (or `refresh()`).": "",
  "The item fields of its value, its name and its colour.": "",
  "An appointment may have several: the field holds a list, the form has a tag box.": "",
  "Appointments take this kind’s colour (else the first kind whose item has one). Their own `color` wins.": "",
  "The item field naming its item of the kind above it in `groups`: nested, a group shows only its own.": "",
  "An item’s own work hours and days; they win over the scheduler’s (the innermost item’s, in nested groups).": "",
  "Whether it may be there (`free`) and what is there: `overlapping`, `blocked`, `offHours`. `options`: `allDay`, `resources` (the values it would have).": "",
  "Its items by kind: `{ field, label, items: { value, text, color, item }[] }[]`.": "",
  "Reads the items again, after you changed them in place.": "",
  "The data layer’s filter for a range, now also for the resources shown (`{ roomId: [1, 2] }`, fields of one value).": "",
  "Now also `resources`: the values its resource fields would get in another group. `cancel` starts `true` where the time is not free; `false` lets it go there.": "",
  "`resources` too.": "",
  "`group`: the resource values of the group it was clicked in.": "",
  "`cell.resources`: the cell’s group; a new appointment there gets them.": ""
}
